#: ../../user_guide.rst:2
msgid "User Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:5
msgid "The window"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:7
msgid "Four regions, left to right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:9
msgid "**Rail** (icon bar)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:10
msgid ""
"Mode buttons — *Library* and *Search* — plus one-shot actions: *Sync*, "
"*Process*, *Import folder*, *Cited Works*, *Settings*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:13
msgid "**Sources**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:14
msgid ""
"One tab per source. Zotero appears as *My Library*; each imported local "
"folder gets its own tab. Inside a tab: library-wide filters at the top "
"(All Papers, Needs Review, Recent, Trash) and the collection tree below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:18
msgid "**Paper list**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:19
msgid ""
"Status, authors, year and title. Click a column header to sort. "
"Ctrl+click a row to reveal which collection it lives in. Right-click for "
"the actions that apply to that paper's current state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:23
msgid "**Detail panel**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:24
msgid ""
"Four tabs — *Metadata*, *PDF*, *Text*, *References*. Each keeps its own "
"scroll position, and the tab you were on is restored when you switch "
"papers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:28
msgid "Sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:31 ../../user_guide.rst:133
msgid "Zotero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:33
msgid ""
"Sync is incremental: only what changed since the last run is fetched. "
"Right-click the *My Library* tab for a **Full Sync** when you want "
"everything re-read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:36
msgid ""
"Sync mirrors Zotero in both directions of removal — items you move to the"
" trash are hidden, items you delete permanently are removed locally too. "
"Collection membership is currently additive: a paper removed from a "
"collection in Zotero keeps its old link here until a full sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:42
msgid "Local folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:44
msgid ""
"Rail → **Import folder** scans a directory tree for PDFs and creates a "
"source tab for it. Files are identified by SHA256, so a PDF already in "
"your Zotero library is linked rather than duplicated — the same paper "
"simply appears under both tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:49
msgid ""
"Right-click a local folder tab → **Remove** to detach it. Papers that "
"exist only in that folder are deleted from the database; papers shared "
"with Zotero just lose the folder link. Files on disk and the OCR cache "
"are never touched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:54
msgid "Processing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:56
msgid ""
"OCR runs against one of three backends, chosen in Settings: RunPod "
"serverless, a direct vLLM pod, or the wrapper API. The wrapper mode keeps"
" the server's queue filled rather than sending one file at a time, and "
"follows the server's own recommendation for how deep to keep that queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:61
msgid ""
"Every PDF is OCR'd, even those with a text layer, so that the corpus is "
"uniform and the results are directly comparable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:64
msgid ""
"Files that are not PDFs — supplementary material, link-only attachments —"
" are marked ``skip`` rather than failing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:67
msgid ""
"If the OCR server becomes unreachable mid-batch, processing pauses rather"
" than failing every remaining file, polls until the server returns, and "
"resumes. The same applies to the extraction batches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:72
msgid "Bibliographic data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:74
msgid ""
"Extraction never overwrites your curated metadata in place. Results live "
"in their own table, tagged with the model that produced them, so you can "
"re-run with a different model and compare."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:78
msgid ""
"What happens after extraction depends on how the result compares with "
"Zotero:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:80
msgid "**Fills gaps only** — applied automatically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:81
msgid "**Agrees with what is there** — recorded as confirmed, no change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:82
msgid "**Disagrees** — the paper is flagged ``rev`` and waits for review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:84
msgid ""
"The review UI is the **Metadata** tab: differing fields get a radio "
"button per side and an editable box, so you can take Zotero's value, take"
" the extracted one, or type a third. Authors are one per line, "
"``Lastname, Firstname``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:88
msgid ""
"If Zotero write-back is enabled, applying pushes the result to Zotero. "
"With it off, changes stay local — and may be overwritten by a later pull "
"sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:92
msgid "References and the citation network"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:94
msgid ""
"Reference extraction locates the bibliography, splits it into entries, "
"and parses each into fields. Entries are then resolved:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:97
msgid "an entry matching a paper you hold becomes a **held** link"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:98
msgid ""
"everything else is canonicalised into a **cited work** node, so the same "
"external paper cited by ten of your papers is one node, not ten rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:101
msgid ""
"The **References** tab shows outgoing references and incoming citations "
"together. Held references are clickable and navigate to the paper. "
"External ones carry a badge showing how many of your papers cite the same"
" work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:105
msgid ""
"Rail → **Cited Works** ranks external works by citation count, with the "
"citing papers listed for each. Right-click a paper → **Show in citation "
"network** for the interactive ego graph: node fill shows direction "
"relative to the focused paper, the border shows whether it is held with a"
" PDF, held without one, or external."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:112
msgid "Search"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:114
msgid ""
"Search runs over the OCR text of every page, and separately over titles "
"and author names, then merges the two. Papers whose *title* matches all "
"your terms rank above papers that merely mention them often — a search "
"for a taxon name finds the monograph about it, not the hundred papers "
"that cite it in passing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:119
msgid "Both plain terms and phrases in quotes work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:122
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:124
msgid "Four tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:126
msgid "OCR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:127
msgid ""
"Backend selection and credentials; queue depth; whether to wait when "
"another machine is already using the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:130
msgid "Biblio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:131
msgid ""
"Automatic and manual extraction toggles (independent), and the LLM "
"backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_guide.rst:134
msgid ""
"Credentials; write-back on/off; OCR JSON upload on/off; automatic parent-"
"item creation for standalone PDFs."
msgstr ""

